  "step1_summary": "• Chief complaint: Constant, worsening lower-midline abdominal (\"tummy\") pain for a few days, rated 8/10.\n• Symptom details:\n  – Onset/duration: Began a few days ago; progressively worse; pain present all the time.\n  – Location: Midline, below the umbilicus (lower abdomen).\n  – Severity: 8/10.\n  – Associated symptoms: Light pink vaginal bleeding after normal period ended 2 weeks ago; occasional nausea (no vomiting); constipation last week (now resolved); small amount of vaginal discharge; no fever, chills, dyspnea, shoulder pain, syncope, dysuria, hematuria, hematochezia, weight loss.\n  – Aggravating/alleviating factors: None specified; pain simply \"gets very bad.\"  \n• Past medical history: No chronic illnesses; no previous surgeries; no prior pregnancies.\n• Medications / allergies: Etonogestrel implant (Implanon) placed 1 year ago; allergic to amoxicillin.\n• Family/social history: 23-year-old female teacher; lives with husband and in-laws; sexually active; no smoking, alcohol, or recreational drugs; travel abroad >1 year ago.\n• Vital signs / exam: Not performed (tele-visit).\n• Labs / imaging: Home pregnancy test negative 1 month ago; no other studies yet. Plan to repeat pregnancy test and schedule in-person abdominal exam.",
